## psc/sema/types/embeds.pengu — promoción de campos de `fundere`.
##
## Un embed es un `SemaField` con `FIELD_EMBED` en el prefijo de campos del
## host, así que la promoción es pura resolución de nombres sobre esa tabla:
## nada de vtable ni de tipos nuevos. Este módulo solo depende de la tabla de
## tipos (no de `SemaState`) para que el codegen use exactamente la misma
## resolución que el checker.
##
## ## Memoria
## `route_into` y `field_type_via` no asignan si no se les pasa una ruta; las
## rutas usan listas owned del llamador.

import psc.sema.types.kind as tk
import psc.sema.types.table as table

## El campo se alcanza (la ruta quedó en `path`).
const ROUTE_FOUND as int is 1
## El campo no existe en el tipo ni en sus embeds.
const ROUTE_NONE as int is 0
## El campo existe en más de un embed: hace falta la ruta explícita.
const ROUTE_AMBIGUOUS as int is -1

## Desenvuelve alias/seal (no `ref`).
##
## ## Memoria
## O(profundidad); no asigna.
weave unwrap with t as ref to table.SemaTypeTable, ty as int into int:
    var cur as int is ty
    var guard as int is 0
    while cur > 0 and guard < 16:
        var st as table.SemaType is calling table.at with t, cur
        if st.kind == tk.SemaTypeKind.TkAlias or st.kind == tk.SemaTypeKind.TkSeal:
            set cur is st.b
        else:
            return cur
        set guard is guard + 1
    return cur

## Índice del campo propio `nid` en `ty` (rune/echo), o `-1`.
##
## ## Memoria
## No asigna.
weave own_field_index with t as ref to table.SemaTypeTable, ty as int, nid as int into int:
    var u as int is calling unwrap with t, ty
    if u <= 0:
        return -1
    var st as table.SemaType is calling table.at with t, u
    if st.kind != tk.SemaTypeKind.TkRune and st.kind != tk.SemaTypeKind.TkEcho:
        return -1
    var info as table.SemaNominalInfo is (t->nominal_infos at st.a)
    var j as int is 0
    while j < info.fields_count:
        var f as table.SemaField is (t->fields at (info.fields_first + j))
        if f.name == nid:
            return j
        set j is j + 1
    return -1

## Tipo de un campo propio (sin promoción); `0` si no existe.
##
## ## Memoria
## No asigna.
weave own_field_type with t as ref to table.SemaTypeTable, ty as int, nid as int into int:
    var j as int is calling own_field_index with t, ty, nid
    if j < 0:
        return 0
    var u as int is calling unwrap with t, ty
    var st as table.SemaType is calling table.at with t, u
    var info as table.SemaNominalInfo is (t->nominal_infos at st.a)
    var f as table.SemaField is (t->fields at (info.fields_first + j))
    return f.type

## `true` si el campo `idx` de `ty` es un embed.
##
## ## Memoria
## No asigna.
weave is_embed_field with t as ref to table.SemaTypeTable, ty as int, idx as int into bool:
    var u as int is calling unwrap with t, ty
    if u <= 0:
        return false
    var st as table.SemaType is calling table.at with t, u
    if st.kind != tk.SemaTypeKind.TkRune and st.kind != tk.SemaTypeKind.TkEcho:
        return false
    var info as table.SemaNominalInfo is (t->nominal_infos at st.a)
    if idx < 0 or idx >= info.fields_count:
        return false
    var f as table.SemaField is (t->fields at (info.fields_first + idx))
    return (f.flags & table.FIELD_EMBED) != 0

## Ruta de embeds que lleva al campo `nid`.
##
## Añade a `path` los `NameId` de los campos-embed que hay que atravesar; el
## último tramo es el campo `nid` dentro del último embed. Una ruta vacía con
## `ROUTE_FOUND` significa campo propio. La regla es la del diseño: el campo
## propio gana; si aparece en exactamente un embed, se promociona; si aparece
## en más de uno, es ambiguo.
##
## ## Memoria
## O(embeds × profundidad); las listas temporales se liberan aquí.
weave route_into with t as ref to table.SemaTypeTable, ty as int, nid as int, path as ref to list of int, depth as int into int:
    if depth > 32:
        return ROUTE_NONE
    if (calling own_field_index with t, ty, nid) >= 0:
        return ROUTE_FOUND
    var u as int is calling unwrap with t, ty
    if u <= 0:
        return ROUTE_NONE
    var st as table.SemaType is calling table.at with t, u
    if st.kind != tk.SemaTypeKind.TkRune and st.kind != tk.SemaTypeKind.TkEcho:
        return ROUTE_NONE
    var info as table.SemaNominalInfo is (t->nominal_infos at st.a)
    var hits as int is 0
    var hit_path as list of int is list of int
    defer banish hit_path
    var i as int is 0
    while i < info.fields_count:
        var f as table.SemaField is (t->fields at (info.fields_first + i))
        if (f.flags & table.FIELD_EMBED) != 0:
            var sub as list of int is list of int
            var r as int is calling route_into with t, f.type, nid, (sigil of sub), depth + 1
            if r == ROUTE_AMBIGUOUS:
                banish sub
                return ROUTE_AMBIGUOUS
            if r == ROUTE_FOUND:
                set hits is hits + 1
                if hits == 1:
                    calling hit_path.push with f.name
                    var k as int is 0
                    while k < sub.len:
                        calling hit_path.push with (sub at k)
                        set k is k + 1
            banish sub
        set i is i + 1
    if hits > 1:
        return ROUTE_AMBIGUOUS
    if hits == 1:
        var k2 as int is 0
        while k2 < hit_path.len:
            calling path.push with (hit_path at k2)
            set k2 is k2 + 1
        return ROUTE_FOUND
    return ROUTE_NONE

## Tipo del campo `nid` siguiendo `path`; `0` si la ruta no lleva a un campo.
##
## ## Memoria
## No asigna.
weave field_type_via with t as ref to table.SemaTypeTable, ty as int, nid as int, path as ref to list of int into int:
    var cur as int is ty
    var i as int is 0
    while i < path->len:
        var step as int is (path at i)
        var nxt as int is calling own_field_type with t, cur, step
        if nxt <= 0:
            return 0
        set cur is nxt
        set i is i + 1
    return calling own_field_type with t, cur, nid

## Tipo del campo `nid` con promoción (sin diagnóstico): `0` si no existe o es
## ambiguo. Los llamadores que tienen un nodo usan `route_into` para emitir
## E0087 antes de caer aquí.
##
## ## Memoria
## Asigna una ruta temporal.
weave field_type_at with t as ref to table.SemaTypeTable, ty as int, nid as int into int:
    var path as list of int is list of int
    defer banish path
    var r as int is calling route_into with t, ty, nid, (sigil of path), 0
    if r != ROUTE_FOUND:
        return 0
    return calling field_type_via with t, ty, nid, (sigil of path)

## `true` si el rune tiene al menos un embed.
##
## ## Memoria
## No asigna.
weave has_embeds with t as ref to table.SemaTypeTable, ty as int into bool:
    var u as int is calling unwrap with t, ty
    if u <= 0:
        return false
    var st as table.SemaType is calling table.at with t, u
    if st.kind != tk.SemaTypeKind.TkRune and st.kind != tk.SemaTypeKind.TkEcho:
        return false
    var info as table.SemaNominalInfo is (t->nominal_infos at st.a)
    var i as int is 0
    while i < info.fields_count:
        var f as table.SemaField is (t->fields at (info.fields_first + i))
        if (f.flags & table.FIELD_EMBED) != 0:
            return true
        set i is i + 1
    return false
